A node taken out of the middle of a ring without relinking its predecessor
leaves the ring running through an empty slot.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: empty slot keeps links
Report: parent's ring does not reach the slot
Report: sibling ring does not close

diff --git a/kernel/cap.c b/kernel/cap.c
--- a/kernel/cap.c
+++ b/kernel/cap.c
@@ -180,7 +180,6 @@ static void detach(struct cap *n, bool adopt)
     if (pred->next & LINK_UP) {
         node(pred->next)->child = (n->next & LINK_UP) ? 0 : n->next;
     } else {
-        pred->next = n->next;
     }
 }
 
